  "body": "From https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1349#issuecomment-640734015 , @chrishtr [proposes spec edits to explicitly specify a preload scanner](https://github.com/chrishtr/rendering/blob/master/stylesheet-loading-proposal.md#preload-scanning-defined) (as one part of a larger proposal on behavior for stylesheet loading). But the proposal doesn't say which exact approach to standardize. I believe this is implemented in slightly different ways:\r\n\r\nGecko: https://web.archive.org/web/20201021003137/https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Gecko/HTML_parser_threading\r\nChromium: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5624#issuecomment-646949323\r\nWebKit: ?\r\n\r\nAre there documents that explain how this is implemented in Chromium and WebKit?\r\n\r\nIs there interest in aligning on the observable behavior here?\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/html-parser @othermaciej @hsivonen @richard-townsend-arm @lilles @mfreed7",
